> I know that this is occasionally suggested, but I think it is not the best
> idea, actually. There are only few scrolls useful if you have them cursed;
> most useful teleportation, but you'll find quite a lot lying around, and
> genocide, only for reverse genociding, which is disputable, and very much
> depends on a specific game. Instead of destroy armor you'd better write
> enchant armor (though writing destroy armor is a bit cheaper). Some other
> scrolls are, if at all, cursed only useful in corner cases (like earth),
> or in rare cases (like remove curse; which is dangerous to use, similar to
> reverse genocide).
> Writing blessed scrolls _whenever you like_, is much more useful; there
> are around 8 scrolls that you even want to have blessed quite always, and
> to use them uncursed (like enchant weapon/armor, to maximize chances for
> enchanting to +7/+5) you can use cursed scrolls.
> 
> My 2 cents.
> 
